FS-07 of the Floor Studio series.

A species dossier is a good page and a dead end. Somebody reads two
thousand words about white oak, decides they like it, and then has to go
and find the thing that shows it to them. Five dossiers and the new-install
head term now carry the floor they are about into Floor Studio, preloaded.

WHITE ASH IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, AND THAT IS THE FEATURE

It has a dossier and no catalogue entry — this company does not currently
lay it. <SeeInMyRoom> validates the configuration and renders NOTHING for
a species that is not in the catalogue, rather than linking into a floor
that cannot be bought. Same rule the renderer obeys, enforced at a
different layer.

THE CTA IS A SERVER COMPONENT AND STAYS ONE

A reference page should not ship a kilobyte of JavaScript so a link can
fire an event. The `src` parameter says which surface sent the visitor and
the studio — already a client island — reports it on arrival.

ON THE HEAD TERM IT SITS ABOVE THE FORM

F-160 put a real <form> above every explanatory section on that page and
that was right. But a visitor on the new-install head term is deciding
what to buy, not only whether to buy, and the cheapest way to move that
decision is to show them the floor in their own room: free, instant, no
contact details. Desire, then confidence, then contact. Putting the form
first only works on the minority who arrived already decided.

docs/FLOOR_STUDIO.md now carries the definition-of-done table, the patch
series and what was built so Phase 2 and Phase 3 are not demolitions.
README names the route and the twin.

pnpm verify green (66 guards), 465 tests.

